---
title: Creamy Pecan Cheesecake
servings: 8
image: https://www.tasteofhome.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Pecan-Pie-Cheesecake_EXPS_FT24_278542_JR_1029_6.jpg
---

> This can very easily be converted to a Walnut Cheesecake if you prefer walnuts.

Toast @pecans{3/4%cup}(coarsely chopped), @pecans{1/3%cup}(coarsely chopped), plus a little extra, in the oven at 325°F, for about ~{10%minutes}.

== Crust ==

In a #food processor{}, combine @graham crackers{1.5%cups}(crushed), @butter{1/2%cup}(softened), and around 1/3 cup of the pecans.

Press the crust mixture into a #9" pie pan{}.

Let chill for at least ~{20%minutes}.

== Filling ==

In a #stand mixer{}, beat @cream cheese{2%8oz packages} until fluffy.

Mix in @sugar{1%cup} until it's smooth, then mix in around 3/4 cup of the toasted pecans.

Spoon the filling into the chilled crust.

Bake at 325°F for ~{20%minutes}, then remove from the oven.

== Topping ==

Increase the oven temperature to 350°F.

Blend @sour cream{1%cup}, @sugar{2%tbsp}, @vanilla{2%tsp}, and @?almond extract{}(to taste) together.

Spread topping over the top of the pie. 

Return the pie to the oven at 350°F for ~{10%minutes}.

After removing the pie from the oven, sprinkle the remaining chopped pecans on top to your preference, or extra crust mixture if you still have it.